@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G11a · The call layer: what a watch contract records
top to bottom direction
hide circle
hide empty methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

class "Operations and their values" as operations #EAF2F8 {
  watch_view receives a watch and length address
  Returns a byte pointer; can write the length
}
class "How a call finishes" as outcomes #FFF1D6 {
  Observable finish and its meaning
  Which outputs the caller may read
}
class "Entities that outlive a call" as entities #F2EDF7 {
  A handle identifies the live watch
  Its lifecycle governs release
}
class "Release responsibility" as responsibility #FFF1D6 {
  Who owes the release
  Calls keep or transfer that duty
}
class "Validity" as validity #E8F3EB {
  Borrowed view: watch must remain alive
  Any earlier invalidator also limits use
}
class "Storage" as storage #E8F3EB {
  The view's bytes have bounds and contents
  The length output has its own storage
}
class "Where and when calls run" as execution #FFF1D6 {
  Permitted entry, overlap and nesting
}
class "Callbacks and their schedules" as callbacks #F2EDF7 {
  notice uses saved context
  Schedule bounds use and states quiescence
}

execution -down-> operations : governs calls
execution -right-> callbacks : governs each\ninvocation
operations -right-> outcomes : each observable finish\nhas an outcome
operations -down-> entities : handles identify
entities -right-> responsibility : lifecycle defines\nhow to discharge the duty
entities -down-> validity : owner's lifetime\nbounds borrowed access
validity -right-> storage : limits when the caller\nmay use the borrowed bytes
operations -up-> callbacks : watch_open registers notice\nand supplies context
callbacks -[hidden]down-> outcomes
outcomes -down-> responsibility : returned obligations\ndepend on the outcome
responsibility -[hidden]down-> storage

legend bottom
  Concept boxes record related facts; labelled arrows read as sentences.
  Arrows show relationships, not transfers, invocations or a timeline.
  Watch contracts are alternatives: a view can have no earlier invalidator,
  or a refreshing watch_view can end it at entry. Callback use can end
  within watch_open or at quiescent destruction of its returned owner.
  Non-normative overview. G11b gathers these facts into a description.
endlegend
@enduml
